# Dark mode UI

All new buttons, inputs, panels, and interactive controls must work in both light and dark mode. Pair every surface/text/border class with a `dark:` variant.

## Reuse shared classes

Import from `frontend/src/lib/buttonStyles.ts` when possible:

- `GHOST_BUTTON_CLASS` — secondary toolbar actions (Refresh, etc.)
- `CANCEL_BUTTON_CLASS` — modal dismiss / cancel
- `ICON_GHOST_BUTTON_CLASS` — icon-only controls
- `TEXT_LINK_CLASS`, `BACK_LINK_CLASS`, `NAV_LINK_CLASS` — text links

## Primary actions

Solid CTAs and submit/send buttons:

```
bg-slate-900 dark:bg-slate-100 text-white dark:text-slate-900
```

Add `hover:opacity-90` and `disabled:opacity-50` as needed.

## Surfaces and text

- Cards/panels: `bg-white dark:bg-slate-900 border-slate-100 dark:border-slate-800`
- Headings: `text-slate-900 dark:text-slate-100`
- Body/muted: `text-slate-700 dark:text-slate-400` or `text-slate-500 dark:text-slate-400`
- Inputs: `bg-slate-50 dark:bg-slate-800 text-slate-900 dark:text-slate-100`

## Accent tints (soft-pink, sage-green)

Use low-opacity backgrounds with dark variants:

- `bg-soft-pink/10 dark:bg-soft-pink/15` (icons, list highlights)
- `bg-soft-pink/15 dark:bg-soft-pink/20` (message bubbles)
- `bg-sage-green/15 dark:bg-sage-green/20` (reply bubbles)

Avoid full `bg-soft-pink text-white` on buttons in dark mode — it reads too bright; prefer the slate primary pattern above.

## Errors and hovers

- Errors: `bg-red-50 dark:bg-red-950/30 text-red-600 dark:text-red-400`
- Hover fills: `hover:bg-slate-100 dark:hover:bg-slate-800`
